        "content": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\n<title>Anatomy of an Active Black Hole - NASA JPL Infographic</title>\n<script>\nwindow.MathJax = { tex: { inlineMath: [['$','$']], displayMath: [['$$','$$']] } };\n</script>\n<script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/mathjax@3/es5/tex-mml-chtml.js\" async></script>\n<style>\n  * { box-sizing: border-box; }\n  body {\n    margin: 0;\n    font-family: 'Segoe UI', Arial, sans-serif;\n    color: #fff;\n    width: 700px;\n  }\n  .header {\n    background: #000;\n    display: flex;\n    align-items: center;\n    padding: 10px 20px;\n    gap: 12px;\n    border-bottom: 3px solid #333;\n  }\n  .header .nasa-logo {\n    width: 50px;\n    height: 40px;\n    background: #0b3d91;\n    color: #fff;\n    display: flex;\n    align-items: center;\n    justify-content: center;\n    font-size: 10px;\n    font-weight: bold;\n    border-radius: 50%;\n    text-align: center;\n  }\n  .header .jpl-text {\n    font-size: 15px;\n    line-height: 1.2;\n  }\n  .header .jpl-text .small {\n    font-size: 11px;\n    font-weight: normal;\n    color: #ccc;\n  }\n\n  section {\n    padding: 25px 30px 35px 30px;\n    position: relative;\n  }\n  h1.section-title {\n    font-size: 24px;\n    margin: 0 0 25px 0;\n    font-weight: 700;\n  }\n\n  /* SECTION 1 - purple */\n  .sec1 { background: #3a1650; }\n  .row1 {\n    display: flex;\n    justify-content: space-between;\n    align-items: flex-start;\n    position: relative;\n  }\n  .circle {\n    border: 2px solid #fff;\n    border-radius: 50%;\n    display: flex;\n    flex-direction: column;\n    align-items: center;\n    justify-content: center;\n    text-align: center;\n    padding: 10px;\n    overflow: hidden;\n    position: relative;\n  }\n  .circle .cap-title { font-weight: bold; font-size: 13px; }\n  .circle .cap-size { font-size: 12px; margin-top: 4px; }\n\n  .placeholder {\n    background: rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\n    border: 1px dashed rgba(255,255,255,0.5);\n    display: flex;\n    align-items: center;\n    justify-content: center;\n    font-size: 11px;\n    color: #ddd;\n    text-align: center;\n    padding: 4px;\n  }\n\n  .bh1 { width: 200px; height: 200px; margin-top: 60px; }\n  .doughnut { width: 170px; height: 170px; margin-top: 90px; }\n  .hostgalaxy { width: 230px; height: 230px; }\n\n  .text1 {\n    font-size: 12px;\n    line-height: 1.5;\n    width: 150px;\n    margin-top: 130px;\n  }\n  .text2 {\n    font-size: 12px;\n    line-height: 1.5;\n    width: 160px;\n    margin-top: 200px;\n    text-align: right;\n  }\n\n  /* SECTION 2 - brown */\n  .sec2 { background: #5a3a1e; }\n  .row2 {\n    display: flex;\n    justify-content: space-between;\n    align-items: center;\n    gap: 15px;\n  }\n  .circle2 {\n    width: 220px;\n    height: 220px;\n  }\n  .row2-text {\n    width: 190px;\n    font-size: 12.5px;\n    line-height: 1.6;\n  }\n  .row2-text p { margin: 0 0 12px 0; }\n  .caption2 {\n    font-size: 12px;\n    text-align: center;\n    width: 220px;\n    margin-top: 8px;\n  }\n  .col2-item { display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: center; }\n\n  /* SECTION 3 - dark blue */\n  .sec3 { background: #16233f; }\n  .galaxy-field {\n    position: relative;\n    height: 480px;\n  }\n  .galaxy-field .placeholder {\n    position: absolute;\n    border-radius: 50%;\n  }\n  .center-text3 {\n    position: absolute;\n    top: 180px;\n    left: 130px;\n    width: 260px;\n    font-size: 13px;\n    line-height: 1.6;\n    text-align: center;\n    z-index: 2;\n  }\n  .center-text3 p { margin: 0 0 12px 0; }\n\n  /* SECTION 4 - dark green */\n  .sec4 { background: #113828; }\n  .row4 {\n    display: flex;\n    gap: 20px;\n    align-items: flex-start;\n  }\n  .col-left {\n    width: 220px;\n    display: flex;\n    flex-direction: column;\n    gap: 10px;\n  }\n  .sat-placeholder { width: 220px; height: 140px; }\n  .col-left p {\n    font-size: 12px;\n    line-height: 1.6;\n    margin: 0;\n  }\n  .col-right {\n    width: 400px;\n    display: flex;\n    flex-direction: column;\n    align-items: center;\n  }\n  .sky-placeholder { width: 400px; height: 320px; }\n  .col-right p {\n    font-size: 12px;\n    line-height: 1.6;\n    margin-top: 10px;\n  }\n</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n\n<div class=\"header\">\n  <div class=\"nasa-logo\">NASA</div>\n  <div class=\"jpl-text\">\n    Jet Propulsion Laboratory<br>\n    <span class=\"small\">California Institute of Technology</span>\n  </div>\n</div>\n\n<!-- SECTION 1 -->\n<section class=\"sec1\">\n  <h1 class=\"section-title\">Anatomy of an Active Black Hole</h1>\n  <div class=\"row1\">\n    <div class=\"circle bh1 placeholder\">\n      <div>\n        <div class=\"cap-title\">Supermassive Black Hole</div>\n        <div class=\"cap-size\">Size: as big as Mercury's orbit</div>\n        <div style=\"margin-top:6px;\">[Photo: black hole with accretion disk]</div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"circle doughnut placeholder\">\n      <div>\n        <div class=\"cap-title\">\"Doughnut\" Ring of Dust &amp; Gas</div>\n        <div class=\"cap-size\">Size: around 1 light-year</div>\n        <div style=\"margin-top:6px;\">[Photo: galaxy core with dust ring]</div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"circle hostgalaxy placeholder\">\n      <div>\n        <div class=\"cap-title\">Host Galaxy</div>\n        <div class=\"cap-size\">Size: about 100,000 light-years</div>\n        <div style=\"margin-top:6px;\">[Photo: host galaxy field]</div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div style=\"display:flex; justify-content: space-between; margin-top: 10px;\">\n    <div class=\"text1\">\n      Astronomers call supermassive black holes and their surrounding disks \"Active Galactic Nuclei\" or \"AGN\"\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"text2\">\n      Black holes emit no light, but the glow from the bright material swirling around them can be seen by telescopes.\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</section>\n\n<!-- SECTION 2 -->\n<section class=\"sec2\">\n  <h1 class=\"section-title\">Why Do Active Black Holes Look Different?</h1>\n  <div class=\"row2\">\n    <div class=\"col2-item\">\n      <div class=\"circle2 placeholder\">[Photo: bright glowing galaxy core, face-on]</div>\n      <div class=\"caption2\">Seen face-on, we detect the light from the hot material surrounding the black hole.</div>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"row2-text\">\n      <p>In some galaxies the black hole regions are <em><strong>incredibly bright</strong></em>, while in other galaxies they appear <em><strong>much darker</strong></em>.</p>\n      <p>A <em>\"unified model\"</em> suggests the angle at which we view them can explain the differences.</p>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"col2-item\">\n      <div class=\"circle2 placeholder\">[Photo: dark dust lane edge-on, doughnut viewed edge-on]</div>\n      <div class=\"caption2\">When viewed through the edge of the dusty doughnut, the black hole is hidden.</div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</section>\n\n<!-- SECTION 3 -->\n<section class=\"sec3\">\n  <h1 class=\"section-title\">What We Expect to See</h1>\n  <div class=\"galaxy-field\">\n    <div class=\"placeholder\" style=\"top:0px; left:0px; width:150px; height:150px; border-radius:50%;\">[Galaxy: bright disk, top-left]</div>\n    <div class=\"placeholder\" style=\"top:20px; left:220px; width:120px; height:60px; border-radius:30px; transform: rotate(-25deg);\">[Galaxy: dark edge-on]</div>\n    <div class=\"placeholder\" style=\"top:0px; left:380px; width:100px; height:100px; border-radius:50%;\">[Galaxy: bright disk]</div>\n    <div class=\"placeholder\" style=\"top:10px; left:540px; width:110px; height:50px; border-radius:25px; transform: rotate(20deg);\">[Galaxy: dark edge-on]</div>\n\n    <div class=\"placeholder\" style=\"top:150px; left:130px; width:100px; height:100px; border-radius:50%;\">[Galaxy: bright disk]</div>\n    <div class=\"placeholder\" style=\"top:170px; left:450px; width:150px; height:150px; border-radius:50%;\">[Galaxy: bright disk]</div>\n\n    <div class=\"placeholder\" style=\"top:330px; left:0px; width:150px; height:70px; border-radius:35px; transform: rotate(-15deg);\">[Galaxy: dark edge-on]</div>\n    <div class=\"placeholder\" style=\"top:320px; left:230px; width:150px; height:150px; border-radius:50%;\">[Galaxy: bright disk, edge-on view]</div>\n    <div class=\"placeholder\" style=\"top:350px; left:440px; width:90px; height:50px; border-radius:25px; transform: rotate(-25deg);\">[Galaxy: dark edge-on]</div>\n    <div class=\"placeholder\" style=\"top:400px; left:570px; width:90px; height:90px; border-radius:50%;\">[Galaxy: bright disk]</div>\n\n    <div class=\"center-text3\">\n      <p>Galaxies are oriented randomly in the sky so the disks in their centers should be oriented randomly as well.</p>\n      <p>Thus we expect to see a random mix of exposed and hidden black holes <em><strong>everywhere we look</strong></em>.</p>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</section>\n\n<!-- SECTION 4 -->\n<section class=\"sec4\">\n  <h1 class=\"section-title\">WISE Observations Challenge \"Unified Model\"</h1>\n  <div class=\"row4\">\n    <div class=\"col-left\">\n      <div class=\"sat-placeholder placeholder\">[Photo: WISE satellite orbiting Earth]</div>\n      <p>Observations with NASA's Wide-field Infrared Survey Explorer reveal that hidden black holes tend to be <em><strong>more clumped together</strong></em> than exposed ones.</p>\n      <p>This violates the \"unified model,\" which predicts we should see the same random distribution of dusty doughnuts regardless of how clumped the objects are.</p>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"col-right\">\n      <div class=\"sky-placeholder placeholder\">[Image: purple clumped galaxy clusters against starfield]</div>\n      <p>Strongly clumped galaxies are likely to have larger halos of dark matter (shown artistically here in purple), which might provide a clue about what else besides the doughnuts could be hiding the black holes.</p>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</section>\n\n</body>\n</html>"
